        <article data-uid="GameFramework.StateMachine.IGameStateMachine">
  
  
  <h1 id="GameFramework_StateMachine_IGameStateMachine" data-uid="GameFramework.StateMachine.IGameStateMachine" class="text-break">
    Interface IGameStateMachine
    
  </h1>
  
  <div class="facts text-secondary">
    <dl><dt>Namespace</dt><dd><a class="xref" href="GameFramework.StateMachine.html">GameFramework.StateMachine</a></dd></dl>
    <dl><dt>Assembly</dt><dd>cs.temp.dll.dll</dd></dl>
  </div>
  
  <div class="markdown summary"><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.StateMachine.IGameStateMachine.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="2" sourceendlinenumber="4">Advanced state machine with constructor injection support.
All dependencies are injected rather than resolved from service locator.
Uses explicit state definitions for maximum Unity compatibility.</p>
<p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.StateMachine.IGameStateMachine.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="6" sourceendlinenumber="8">Design: State machine pattern with async support and transition validation
Pros: Robust state management, prevents invalid transitions, supports complex state logic, Unity compatible
Cons: More complex than simple state switching, requires careful transition planning, explicit state definitions</p>
</div>
